❌ **EDIT: NOT MERGING THIS PR, but still needs to be fixed. new approach to fix deinit is needed. see comments.** ❌

This solves: https://github.com/espressif/esp-idf/issues/9974, and https://github.com/espressif/esp-idf/issues/9877

**Main Changes (to solve the deadlock):** 
- Implements: `usb_serial_jtag_unblock_reads();` & `uart_unblock_reads();` which causes any pending read() to return -1 with **EWOULDBLOCK**. 
- Implement `vRingbufferUnblockRx` which is what the above functions are wait on
- calling`esp_console_repl_X_delete()` unblocks and safely exits the linenoise thread, before we stop the console. This lets the linenoise thread let go of the _readLock, so that we can deinit.
- **linenoise.c**, read operations now return early if **EWOULDBLOCK** is returned by the read operation. This is necessary for linenoise to exit when we deinit.

**The crux of the deadlock fix is here:**

**esp_console_replc.**
```
static esp_err_t esp_console_repl_usb_serial_jtag_delete(esp_console_repl_t *repl) {
    ....
    // wait for repl thread to stop, if it is running
    if (repl_com->state == CONSOLE_REPL_STATE_START) {
        repl_com->state = CONSOLE_REPL_STATE_REPL_STOP_REQUESTED;
        while (repl_com->state != CONSOLE_REPL_STATE_REPL_TASK_ENDED) {
            usb_serial_jtag_unblock_reads();
            vTaskDelay(20 / portTICK_PERIOD_MS);
        }
    } 
    ...
}
```

